# Gulp Starter — AI Rules

## Project Identity
This is a **Gulp 5 starter template** for HTML/CSS/JS development.
Technology stack: Pug, SCSS, TypeScript, Webpack, Browser-sync.

## CRITICAL: What NOT to do
- NEVER add `any` type in TypeScript — strict mode is enabled
- NEVER use `@import` in SCSS — only `@use`
- NEVER use relative imports like `../../../` in TS — always use `@/` alias
- NEVER inline styles in JS — use CSS classes
- NEVER create new components if reusable ones exist (Accordion, Tabs, Dropdowns patterns exist in git history)
- NEVER use `var` — only `const`/`let`
- NEVER commit `build/` or `node_modules/`
- NEVER use ID selectors (`#header`) in CSS — use classes

## Architecture Rules
- All TypeScript components MUST extend `Base` class from `@/components/Base`
- Components use `data-js-*` attributes for DOM selectors, NEVER style classes
- Component structure: `constructor()` → `super()` → `init()` → `bindEvents()`
- Always check element existence before use (`if (!element) { console.error(...); return }`)
- Clean up event listeners on destroy (removeEventListener)

## SCSS Rules
- Use BEM: `.block`, `.block__element`, `.block__parent-child`
- Max nesting: 3 levels
- States: `.is-active`, `.is-hidden`
- JS hooks: `.js-*` prefix
- Use `rem()` function for all sizes (based on 16px root)
- Media queries via mixins: `@include tablet { }`, `@include mobile { }`, `@include hover { }`
- Z-index via `z('layer-name')` function from `_z-index.scss`

## Pug Rules
- Data from `src/markup/data/*.json` available as `jsonData.filename`
- Use `+icon('icon-name')` mixin for SVG icons
- Use `+picture('img/photo.jpg')` mixin for responsive images
- Comments: `//-` (not rendered in HTML)
- All pages extend `layouts/_default.pug`

## File Locations
- New page: `src/markup/pages/page-name.pug`
- New component: `src/scripts/components/ComponentName/index.ts`
- New styles: `src/styles/blocks/_block-name.scss`
- New icon (mono): `src/assets/icons/mono/icon-name.svg`
- New icon (multi): `src/assets/icons/multi/icon-name.svg`
- New image: `src/assets/images/image-name.jpg`
- New font: `src/assets/fonts/FontName.woff2`
- New data: `src/markup/data/file-name.json`

## Build Commands
- `npm run dev` — dev server with hot-reload
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run proxy` — browser-sync proxy mode
- `npm run format` — prettier formatting

## Important Notes
- Critical CSS: important above-the-fold styles go in `src/styles/critical.scss`
- In dev mode critical CSS is linked as separate file; in prod it's inlined in `<head>`
- Webpack uses SWC (not Babel) — 5-10x faster
- SVG sprites generated automatically from `icons/mono/` and `icons/multi/`
- Images auto-optimized + WebP + AVIF generated
- Node.js >= 22 required
